MVX: quarantine unqualified RRC-DQP private controls

This generated artifact preserves the RRC-DQP changes published in CIX's
`cix_opensource__vpu_driver` `p1_7.0_v1.0.2` release at commit
5b9b07b44abcbb5548273995a17893cf3ff3e7f2. It adds two private V4L2 integer
controls, session state and firmware message types 36 and 37 for an RRC-DQP
range and step. The matched protocol-3.5 firmware is available, and the
control defaults are inert until userspace explicitly sets them.

The matched CIX 2026Q2 Multimedia SDK's control header and tools expose no
consumer for either control. No public contract defines their units, codec
scope, interaction with other rate-control settings or expected observable
effect. Matching firmware binaries establish protocol availability, not those
semantics or a usable userspace ABI. Enabling undocumented private control IDs
would therefore add collision and ABI-drift risk without demonstrated
end-user functionality.

The 7.1 ebuild consequently retains this source-faithful artifact for review
but does not apply it by default. Re-enable it only when a named, matched
firmware and userspace release documents the contract and its behavior can be
qualified. Patches 71150 and 71160 are deliberately independent and apply to
the post-71130 tree. Both the omitted and applied forms have passed exact
patch replay and focused build validation.

